  "live_records": {
    "q-67258": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67258",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the $1$st term is $0$ and the $9$th term is $40.$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe already know that the first term is ${a}_{1}=0,$ so we just need to figure out the common difference $d.$ \n\nTo find the common difference, we can find the total difference between the terms ${a}_{1}=0$ and ${a}_{9}=40$ and divide it by the number of jumps, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{9}-{a}_{1}}{9-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{40-0}{9-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{8} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =0+(n-1)(5) \\\\  & =5n-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
