    "q-5430": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5430",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the general formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence if the $7$th term is $-18$ and the first term is $6.$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d.\n$$\n\nWe already know that the first term is ${a}_{1}=6,$ so we just need to figure out the common difference $d.$ \n\nTo find the common difference, we can find the total difference between the terms ${a}_{1}=6$ and ${a}_{7}=-18$ and divide it by the number of jumps, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{7}-{a}_{1}}{7-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-18-6}{7-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24}{6} \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,  the formula for the $n$th term of our arithmetic sequence is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =6+(n-1)(-4) \\\\  & =6-4n+4 \\\\  & =10-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
