    "q-67315": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67315",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The second and third terms of an arithmetic sequence are $45$ and $80,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence.",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by  \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nSince the terms ${a}_{2}=45$ and ${a}_{3}=80$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{3}-{a}_{2} \\\\  & =80-45 \\\\  & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{2}=45,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{2}$ is $1$ jump after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+1\\cdot d \\\\ 45 & ={a}_{1}+35 \\\\ 45-35 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =10+(n-1)\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =10+35n-35 \\\\  & =35n-25\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-67315-a",
