    "q-177698": {
      "dom_id": "step-q177698",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The $7$th and $8$th terms of an arithmetic sequence are $-13$ and $-20,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence.",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nSince the terms ${a}_{7}=-13$ and ${a}_{8}=-20$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{8}-{a}_{7} \\\\  & =-20-(-13) \\\\  & =-20+13 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{8}=-20,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{8}$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ -20 & ={a}_{1}+7(-7) \\\\ -20 & ={a}_{1}-49 \\\\ -20+49 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =29.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =29+(n-1)(-7) \\\\  & =29-7n+7 \\\\  & =36-7n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
